-- StreetRise — Migration 046: GoPasco (Pasco County) static GTFS
--
-- NOT APPLIED. Runbook: docs/apply-migrations-042-046.md.
-- Requires migration 042 (the tables).
--
-- 945 stops, 14 routes from GoPasco's published bundle, feed 20260828
-- (valid 2026-08-29 → 2031-12-13). Generated by
-- `scripts/build-transit-sql.ts`; DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
--
-- ── This feed has no calendar.txt at all ────────────────────
-- GoPasco publishes NO weekly service patterns. Every operating day is an
-- explicit `calendar_dates.txt` row — 1,657 of them, all exception_type 1
-- (added), running out to 2031. GTFS permits this and the importer now
-- handles it: where `calendar.txt` does not describe a service on the
-- reference date, the day pattern is inferred from the dates the service is
-- actually scheduled to run over the following four weeks.
--
-- Only services calendar.txt is silent about are inferred this way. Where a
-- weekly pattern exists it wins, because folding holiday exceptions into it
-- would corrupt it — HART adds its SUNDAY service on Labor Day, a Monday, and
-- reading that as "runs on Mondays" would mark Sunday-only stops as having
-- weekday service.
--
-- ── Pasco has no Sunday service ─────────────────────────────
-- The inference produces exactly two services: one running Mon–Fri, one
-- running Saturdays. Not one of the 945 stops has Sunday service, and the
-- generated rows say so — `serves_sunday` is FALSE across the board.
--
-- That is precisely the kind of thing this whole table exists to surface. A
-- Sunday meal service in Pasco County cannot be reached by bus by anyone
-- without a car, and until now nothing in StreetRise could say so.
--
-- ── Current listings ────────────────────────────────────────
-- StreetRise has two public Pasco listings today, both campgrounds, and both
-- are genuinely remote: Jay B. Starkey Wilderness Park is 2.4 km from the
-- nearest stop and Withlacoochee River Park is 6.1 km. Neither is raised by
-- the backfill below, correctly — they will instead render the amber
-- "nearest GoPasco stop is about 1.5 mi away" line, which is the honest and
-- more useful answer.
--
-- `fare_attributes.txt` ships with a header and no rows, so every route lands
-- fare_price NULL / is_fare_free FALSE — unknown, not free.
-- ================================================================


